# L §4.6 steps 2 and 3, §6.4 (tally 2.1.7 R4, issue #143; #137): a scenario's replace of a base reading stands
# above the base whatever the known dates: known the base's day (same) or before it (early), 200.00 PLN. 2.1.6's
# refcore weighed known dates across the layers and kept the base's 100.00 PLN. (T's C14 vectors.)
=== base.tally
model rd
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T C14 (invented): a scenario's replace of a base reading at the same instant, its version known the base's day or earlier; it wins whatever the known dates (L §6.4, §4.6 step 2; issue #137)"

source card "invented"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-02-28) in rd

ask qs: bal(konto, 2026-02-28) in same

ask qe: bal(konto, 2026-02-28) in early

version v
  cite card
  governs 2026-01..2026-02
  known 2026-03-05
  anchor konto
  opening[konto] = 0 at 2026-01-01 start "base"
  stated[konto] = 100 at 2026-02-28 end "base"
=== same.tally
scenario same over rd
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01
  note "T C14 (invented): its version known the base's day (issue #137)"

version same_v
  cite card
  governs 2026-01..2026-02
  known 2026-03-05
  anchor konto
  replace stated[konto] = 200 at 2026-02-28 end "the scenario"
=== early.tally
scenario early over rd
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01
  note "T C14 (invented): its version known before the base's (issue #137)"

version early_v
  cite card
  governs 2026-01..2026-02
  known 2026-03-01
  anchor konto
  replace stated[konto] = 200 at 2026-02-28 end "the scenario"
=== expect
q: 100.00 PLN
  world: rd
  anchor: konto 2026-02-28 end, stated 100.00 PLN, difference 100.00 PLN
  cut 2026-03-10
qe: 200.00 PLN
  world: early
  anchor: konto 2026-02-28 end, stated 200.00 PLN, difference 200.00 PLN
  cut 2026-03-10
qs: 200.00 PLN
  world: same
  anchor: konto 2026-02-28 end, stated 200.00 PLN, difference 200.00 PLN
  cut 2026-03-10
